then `r + r'` identifies `X` with `Z`. -/
theorem relabellingSet_add {X Y Z : DiscreteMetricDatum N S D δ} {r r' : ℝ}
    (hr : r ∈ relabellingSet X Y) (hr' : r' ∈ relabellingSet Y Z) :
    r + r' ∈ relabellingSet X Z := by
  obtain ⟨hr0, e, he, hb⟩ := hr
  obtain ⟨hr0', e', he', hb'⟩ := hr'
  refine ⟨add_nonneg hr0 hr0', e' * e, ?_, fun i j => ?_⟩
  · -- (e' * e) (base X) = base Z
    simp [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, he, he']  -- need to check
  · calc |dist X i j - dist Z ((e'*e) i) ((e'*e) j)|
      = |(dist X i j - dist Y (e i) (e j)) + (dist Y (e i) (e j) - dist Z (e' (e i)) (e' (e j)))| := by ring_nf
      _ ≤ |dist X i j - dist Y (e i) (e j)| + |dist Y (e i) (e j) - dist Z (e' (e i)) (e' (e j))| := abs_add _ _
      _ ≤ r + r' := add_le_add (hb i j) (hb' (e i) (e j))
```

Note `e' * e` on `Equiv.Perm (Fin N)`: multiplication is composition; `(e' * e) i = e' (e i)`. Applying to basepoint: `(e'*e) (base X) = e' (e (base X)) = e' (base Y) = base Z`. `simp [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, he, he']` should work or `rw [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, he, he']`.

